    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0299" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4478: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-14T23:00:00+01:00">July 14, 1931—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 15—5:43 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>83. Reference is made to my telegram No. 79, July 13, 10 a.m.<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d130-f1"/> The Belgian Legation at Berlin has informed the Belgian
                    Government that discussions with regard to Belgian-German questions have been
                    initiated in Berlin by the German Government. These conversations will be
                    continued at London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
